# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials. The endpoint key lives in .env and must never be committed; the
# repository is intended to be released anonymously alongside the paper.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*_key.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated outputs. These are large and reproducible from the scripts; the
# paper's numbers are reproduced by running the pipeline, not by shipping its
# results. The two exceptions below are kept deliberately.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
outputs*/
result_*/
plan_transfer/
ablation_*/
traces/
n60/
*.log

# Keep the evaluation manifests and the measured numbers the paper cites, since
# a reader checking a table should not have to re-run 1500 API calls to see the
# raw judgements behind it.
!outputs_n60/style_ab.csv
!outputs_n60/style_ab_summary.csv
!outputs_n60/framing_audit.csv
!outputs_n60/idsim_validation.csv
!**/preservation_metrics.csv
!**/index.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights and caches. face_landmarker.task is the exception: it is 3.8 MB
# and the evaluation machine has no CDN access, so shipping it is what makes the
# preservation metrics runnable offline.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.bin
!assets/models/face_landmarker.task
.cache/
~/.insightface/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch. third_party/*/output holds per-run intermediates from the baselines.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
third_party/*/output/
third_party/*/_sample_*.txt
*.orig
*.pre_lazy
.idsim_tmp.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored third-party systems (143 MB, and GenArtist carries its own .git).
# These are other people's repositories; we ship the patches we had to make to
# run them, not copies of them. scripts/setup_third_party.sh clones the upstream
# commits and applies patches/, so a reader reproduces the baseline rather than
# trusting our snapshot of it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
third_party/
!third_party/README.md
!patches/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The full image corpus (368 MB). The evaluation set actually used by the paper
# lives in compare/ and is committed: ten content images, six styles, and the
# manifests that pair them. data/ is the pool those were drawn from and is not
# needed to reproduce any reported number.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Evaluation imagery is NOT redistributed.
#
# The content images are photographs of real people and were not collected for
# public release; the style references are third-party artworks whose licences we
# have not cleared for redistribution. Shipping them would put a rights question
# on every reader who clones this repository, and it is not ours to answer on
# their behalf.
#
# What ships instead is the manifest: compare/pairs*.txt names every pair, its
# stylistic dimension, and the exact file each side expects. Point those paths at
# your own images, or at the corresponding public datasets, and every script in
# scripts/ runs unchanged. README.md explains the arrangement.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
compare/content*/
compare/style*/
compare/paper_results*/
compare/**/*.jpg
compare/**/*.jpeg
compare/**/*.png
!compare/paper_results/pairs.txt
assets/*.jpg
assets/*.png
!assets/models/

# Stray working directories and pulled analysis files that are not part of the
# release. traces*/ is per-run instrumentation; the CSVs the paper cites live
# under outputs_n60/ and are whitelisted above.
traces*/
/outputs_n60_framing_audit.csv
